  "description": "Outpaint via an OpenAI-compatible /v3/images/edits API served by OpenVINO Model Server",
  "extendedDescription": "Uses the same OVMS /v3/images/edits endpoint as inpainting. Open **Outpaint Canvas** to place your image on the target resolution; transparent areas become the generation mask (OVMS outpaint semantics). The composite is uploaded as one PNG with alpha. Serve an inpainting-capable model on OVMS (default stable-diffusion-v1-5/stable-diffusion-inpainting). Default API base URL http://127.0.0.1:8000/v3. Without opening the canvas (or with no transparent border), the node uses image-to-image (strength + rng_seed) if the mask is empty\u2014use a base diffusion model on OVMS for that path.",
  "mediaType": "image",
  "toolCategory": "edit-images",
  "toolInstructions": "Load a source image, open **Outpaint Canvas**, position and scale it on the canvas (transparent areas are filled by the model), then describe what should appear in those areas. Match size to your OVMS model.",
